            <div xml:id="d987">

                <pb facs="0868" n="752" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg752"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/3280.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the American Consul at Frontera</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-03-19T17:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 19, 1912—5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>You may circulate the President’s proclamation, March 2, as you propose, but its
                    language should be in nowise altered and great discretion should be used.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Huntington Wilson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
